  "id": "presbyopia",
  "term": "presbyopia",
  "definition": "Presbyopia is an age-related problem in the eye’s focusing system in which the lens becomes less able to bring near objects into clear focus. It commonly causes increasing difficulty with close-up tasks such as reading, and the need for near-vision help can also be influenced by factors like viewing distance and depth of focus.",
